#: ../../../projectconf/sections/env/options/upload/upload_command.rst:19
msgid ""
"Override default :ref:`platforms` upload command with a custom command. You "
"can pass a full upload command with arguments and options or mix with :ref:"
"`projectconf_upload_flags`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projectconf/sections/env/options/upload/upload_command.rst:22
msgid ""
"In order to use ``upload_command``, ``upload_protocol = custom`` must be "
"specified."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projectconf/sections/env/options/upload/upload_command.rst:24
msgid ""
"Default upload commands are declared in ``builder/main.py`` script file of :"
"ref:`platforms`. See a list with open source :ref:`platforms` => https://"
"github.com/topics/platformio-platform"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projectconf/sections/env/options/upload/upload_command.rst:29
msgid ""
"Please note that you can use build variables in ``upload_command``, such as "
"PlatformIO project folders and other runtime configuration. A list with "
"build variables are available by running ``pio run --target envdump`` "
"command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projectconf/sections/env/options/upload/upload_command.rst:34
msgid "**Examples**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projectconf/sections/env/options/upload/upload_command.rst:36
msgid ""
"Override default upload command but handle pre-uploading actions (looking "
"for serial port, extra image preparation, etc.). Normally, the pre-"
"configured upload options will be stored in ``$UPLOADERFLAGS`` build "
"variable. A classic default upload command for :ref:`platforms` may look as "
"``some-flash-bin-tool $UPLOADERFLAGS $SOURCE``, where ``$SOURCE`` will be "
"replaced by a real program/firmware binary."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projectconf/sections/env/options/upload/upload_command.rst:43
msgid ""
"``${platformio.packages_dir}`` template points to :ref:"
"`projectconf_pio_packages_dir`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projectconf/sections/env/options/upload/upload_command.rst:65
msgid "Override default upload command and skip pre-uploading actions."
msgstr ""
